  "final_message": "I have started running the tests to verify the baseline and will proceed as soon as the test run finishes.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this change is blocked\n\n1. **Breaking external contracts**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published across repository boundaries to downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` directly is a breaking schema change that violates ARCH-4's requirement that changes be additive.\n2. **Model coupling**: Removing `channel` from the domain [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model and [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) builder would prevent this service from publishing the contract required by existing consumers during the deprecation period.\n\n### Recommended deprecation procedure\n\nTo retire `channel` in compliance with ARCH-4:\n\n1. **Deprecation**: Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L23).\n2. **Consumer migration**: Update downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to remove dependencies on `channel` or make handling of the field optional.\n3. **Removal in a new schema version**: Once all deployed consumers have migrated, increment `schemaVersion` on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L9) and drop the field following team deprecation timelines.\n",
